  "summary": "Sun Yat-sen was born on 12 November 1866 in a village in Xiangshan County, Guangdong, and became a leading figure of China's republican revolution. He took up the post of provisional president of the Republic of China at Nanjing in January 1912, and died on 12 March 1925.",
